e-handling-requirements walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the Aster Diagnostics handling matrix authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Aster Diagnostics (continued from e-asset-classification); four tiers
Public / Internal / Confidential / Restricted. All company facts fictional.
Artifacts authored:
  - Handling matrix: 4 tiers x 5 dimensions (labeling, storage, transmission, disposal,
    retention hook); one rule per cell
  - Disposal column cites SP 800-88 Rev. 2 clear/purge/destroy per tier + media type,
    with verifier and record named
  - Testability check: every cell assigned a sampling method + frequency
      (labeling: quarterly doc sampling; storage: DLP scans; transmission: egress log
      review + DLP blocks; disposal: sanitization records before asset sign-off)
  - Exception process: written request, time-bounded, owner-approved, compensating
    controls named (one paragraph)
Design decisions recorded in lesson §3:
  1. Email attachments banned for Restricted (secure file transfer w/ access logging)
  2. "No local copies, period" for Restricted + documented exception path
  3. Disposal methods cite 800-88 Rev. 2 by name; verification is part of the rule
  4. Every cell got a check — three cells honesty-passed for testability

